{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787080108,"nonce":"QzWhFirjXqlmkRHV7Lrh+ONwics=","title":"A snooze reaches Slack as a red `:fire: Firing` card, so the moment oto agrees to go quiet is rendered as the alert it agreed to stop mentioning","message":"**What is wrong.** `snoozed` and `unsnoozed` are real Reasons (`internal/notification/domain/reason.go:65-67`) and they are the only two a snooze may not suppress — `SnoozeExempt` (`:315`), because *\"a snooze that cannot announce its own beginning and end is the silent suppression §B.6 forbids\"*. So oto is right to speak. What it says is wrong. The Slack renderer has **no `snoozed` branch at all**: `replyBody` falls to its `default:` arm and draws `:information_source: *Title* — \u003cstatus\u003e`, where `\u003cstatus\u003e` is the group's state — `:fire: Firing` — on `CardFiring`'s red `#a30200` attachment bar, with no footer clause naming why the card moved. A human asking oto to be quiet about a still-firing signal gets, in the same thread, a red card announcing that the signal is firing.\n\n**The demonstration.** It is frozen in two checked-in goldens, and they were checked in *because the bytes are wrong* (`internal/channels/render/slack/golden_test.go:677-716`). `testdata/reply_snoozed.golden.json` is eight lines of proof: `\"reason\": \"snoozed\"` in the metadata, `\"color\": \"#a30200\"`, and the single rendered block reading `\":information_source: *OtoSmokeTest* — :fire: Firing\"`. The fallback text — the string a phone notification shows — is `\":bell: Update on: OtoSmokeTest on smoke-test. Severity critical, team observability, firing since 17:56 UTC.\"` The word \"snooze\" appears nowhere in either card. `testdata/root_snoozed.golden.json` is the amended root, equally silent.\n\nThat both cards are delivered follows from `PlanFor` without a single snooze-aware line. `rootModeFor` (`internal/notification/domain/mode.go:80-98`) names only `comment` and `unacked_reminder` in its switch, so `snoozed` takes `default:` and gets `update_root`; `hasReply` (`:110-119`) excludes only `fired`, `some_resolved`, `repeat` and `unacked`, so `snoozed` gets a `thread_reply` too. Both are then ungatable: `ungatedReplies` (`internal/notification/domain/verbosity.go:88-95`) lists `ReasonSnoozed` and `ReasonUnsnoozed`, which §H.6 states as *\"always — exempt from snooze suppression (§B.8.4)\"*. So the pair lands at every verbosity, on every destination, today.\n\nAnd nothing in the card *could* say otherwise, because the view has no snooze axis to render. `NotificationView` carries no snoozed-until and no snoozer; `CaseView` (`internal/channels/domain/view.go:102-114`) has `SuppressionReason` — which is Alertmanager's, explicitly *\"NOT\"* oto's (`internal/notification/domain/suppression.go:6-11`) — and nothing else. `SuppressedSnoozed` lives in oto's own notification-suppression vocabulary, so `CardSuppressed` never fires and the colour stays firing-red by construction. `TrailEntry.Kind` has no `snoozed` verb either, so `trailVerb` would print the raw word.\n\n**Why it matters.** This is SPEC §B.6's fatal shape with a message attached. §B.6's rule is that oto's silence must never be indistinguishable from \"there was no alert\"; here oto has gone one worse and rendered its own quiet as the loudest thing it draws. The operator who snoozed sees the card they were trying to silence get redder. The channel around them sees a firing critical they will now ask about. And `unsnoozed` is the same defect from the other side — the one card whose entire content is \"oto is audible again\" is indistinguishable from every other update.\n\nThe renderer is not where the fix starts. A `snoozed` branch with nothing to read would say \"Snoozed\" and stop — no until-when, no by-whom, no reason — which is a different wrong card. The view has to carry the snooze first.\n\n**Where.** `internal/channels/render/slack/reply.go` (`replyBody`'s switch; there is no `reasonSnoozed` arm to point at, which is the defect) · `internal/channels/render/slack/testdata/reply_snoozed.golden.json` and `root_snoozed.golden.json` (the frozen evidence) · `internal/channels/render/slack/golden_test.go:677-726` (the chain, written out, and `snoozedView`) · `internal/notification/domain/mode.go:80-98`, `:110-119` (`PlanFor`'s default treatment) · `internal/notification/domain/verbosity.go:88-95` (`ungatedReplies`) · `internal/channels/domain/view.go:50-114` (`GroupView`, `CaseView` — where a snooze axis would go) · `internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:183-194` (`SnoozedUntil` on the snapshot, which the view does not carry forward) · `docs/design/SPEC.md` §B.6, §B.8.3–B.8.4, §H.6.\n\n**Scope.** large, and honestly so. It is not a renderer branch. It needs a snooze axis added to `NotificationView` and `CaseView` (until-when, actor, note), the snapshot's `SnoozedUntil` and the actor carried through `ViewService.project`, a `snoozed`/`unsnoozed` arm in `replyBody` and in the root card's status derivation, a card colour that is neither firing-red nor `CardSuppressed` (a snooze is not an upstream silence and must not be drawn as one), a `TrailEntry.Kind` verb, and the words themselves — which are a product decision, not an implementation one. It touches `notification/domain`, `notification/service`, `channels/domain` and `channels/render/slack`, and it re-cuts two goldens that exist to make the current bytes visible.\n\n**Done when.** A `snoozed` reply says a human snoozed this, until when, and who — and does not say the alert is firing. Neither card is firing-red. `unsnoozed` says oto is audible again and is distinguishable from a state change. `reply_snoozed.golden.json` and `root_snoozed.golden.json` are re-cut and the comment above them at `golden_test.go:677` no longer describes them as evidence of a defect. `NotificationView` carries the snooze as a fact rather than leaving the renderer to infer one it cannot see, and the fallback text — the string that reaches a phone — names the snooze rather than the firing.","files":null}]}